summary: Race condition vulnerability in file handling of sudoedit SELinux RBAC support
description: |
    Verify that sudoedit with SELinux RBAC support is not vulnerable to a
    symbolic link race condition attack, ensuring it does not segfault and does
    not allow file ownership changes through a malicious EDITOR variable.
contact: Martin Zelený <mzeleny@redhat.com>
component:
- sudo
test: ./runtest.sh
recommend:
- sudo
duration: 10m
enabled: true
tag:
- Tier1
- CI-Tier-1
adjust:
-   enabled: false
    when: distro < rhel-8
    continue: false
-   enabled: false
    when: distro == rhel-alt-7
    continue: false
extra-nitrate: TC#0609476
extra-summary: /CoreOS/sudo/Regression/symbolic-link-attack-in-SELinux-enabled-sudoedit
extra-task: /CoreOS/sudo/Regression/symbolic-link-attack-in-SELinux-enabled-sudoedit
